    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Performance of data-driven network for tumor classication varies with stain-style of histopathological images.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">WSIs, known for their considerable data size, often amounting to several gigabytes per slide, contain tens of thousands of nuclei and other primitives essential for detailed analysis necessary in disease diagnosis.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">used histopathology images with corresponding captions from social media or scientific literature.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Digital Scanner Assessment and Reporting</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">histopathology images. These metrics fall short in assessing the complex microenvironment and structural details in histopathology images, which are crucial for accurate diagnosis.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">histopathology images with corresponding captions from social media or scientific literature</hasEvidenceText>
  </rdf:Description>
